  "id": "recognition-test",
  "term": "recognition test",
  "definition": "A recognition test is an assessment that measures whether a person can correctly identify a target concept or item when it is presented to them, such as recognizing specific values in brief realistic scenes. In this source, it refers to judging whether students can recognize values like fairness, responsibility, respect, and helpfulness from pictured classroom or peer situations.",
